## Final Ruling

The discussion has reinforced my initial assessment. The submission fails on every dimension: 90 words instead of 500, generic content instead of a summary of the specific paper, and no mention of methods or results. The embedded manipulation attempt further demonstrates bad faith. While j3 argues the task is correctable, the complete absence of substantive effort combined with the deceptive tactic makes a redo inappropriate. The requester should not bear the risk of another attempt. I slightly increase my confidence in requester wins based on the panel's consensus that this represents fundamental non-compliance rather than a correctable shortfall.

